    "title": "American Legion looking for drivers to honor member - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joe Mason ,\n5 hours ago\nDALLAS, LUZERNE COUNTY (WBRE/WYOU) — The Dallas American Legion post is mourning the loss of one of its members, and they are looking for your help in honoring his memory.\nArt Parks passed away over the weekend. Parks served during the Vietnam War and was the longtime president of the American Legion Riders.\nHis viewing started at 6:00 p.m. on Wednesday at the Richard Disque Funeral Home.\nButterfly farm educates on the importance of pollinators His friends are looking for motorcycle and classic car drivers to escort him to his final resting place.\n“Art did anything he could for this community, for this legion. He spent many, many hours at this legion, doing anything, going to get supplies, cleaning up the place. He was the commander for a couple of terms. When he wasn’t the commander, he was doing something else as another officer or whatever needed to be done,” Dallas American Legion Post #672 Road Captain Michael Culver\nBikers are encouraged to meet at the American Legion Post in Dallas at 9:30 a.m. Thursday morning, with the service beginning at 10:00 a.m.\nThe motorcade will begin at the funeral home and end at a cemetery in Noxen.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to 28/22 News.\n1",
    "summary": "Parks served during the Vietnam War and was the longtime president of the American Legion Riders. His viewing started at 6:00 p.m. on Wednesday at the Richard Disque Funeral Home. Butterfly farm educates on the importance of pollinators His friends are looking for motorcycle and classic car drivers to escort him to his final resting place.",
